{"analytics_identifier":null,"base_path":"/government/news/pm-meeting-with-president-zelenskyy-of-ukraine-14-october-2026","content_id":"1b56ddd2-2d92-475a-bad5-629c5a55c472","description":"The Prime Minister welcomed President Volodymyr Zelenskyy of Ukraine to Downing Street this afternoon.","details":{"attachments":[],"body":"<div class=\"govspeak\"><p>The Prime Minister welcomed President Volodymyr Zelenskyy of Ukraine to Downing Street this afternoon.</p>\n\n<p>The leaders began by reflecting on their call on Saturday, and Russia’s blatant indiscriminate attacks on civilians and energy infrastructure since President Trump called for an energy ceasefire.</p>\n\n<p>It was clear that Russia had no interest in peace, the leaders underlined.</p>\n\n<p>Turning to how Ukraine’s allies could step up support, particularly in response to Russia’s barrage of jet-powered drones, the Prime Minister set out the UK’s latest package of Lightweight Multirole Missiles.</p>\n\n<p>The UK would continue to develop innovative military solutions for use on the battlefield in Ukraine, including retrofitting British capability onto equipment gifted from other partners, the Prime Minister added.</p>\n\n<p>On long range missiles, the leaders discussed how the UK could accelerate defensive support to Ukraine ahead of the winter.</p>\n\n<p>The UK would also continue its diplomatic efforts to support international supplies of defensive equipment too, the Prime Minister added.</p>\n\n<p>Both looked forward to speaking again soon.</p>\n</div>","change_history":[{"note":"First published.","public_timestamp":"2026-10-14T18:43:00Z"}],"emphasised_organisations":["705dbea4-8bd7-422e-ba9c-254557f77f81"],"images":[{"caption":null,"content_type":"image/jpeg","sources":{"s216":"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5a37daeae5274a79051c91fb/s216_number10.jpg","s300":"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5a37dae940f0b649cceb1841/s300_number10.jpg","s465":"https://assets.publishing.serv